# Testing

## Stack and intent
- Use Vitest + React Testing Library.
- Test behavior users can observe, not implementation details.
- Focus coverage on critical business logic and shared design-system components.
- Do not write filler tests only to raise coverage metrics.

## Coverage expectations
- Cover loading, success, error, and disabled states when relevant.
- Add a regression test for every bug fix.
- Mock API calls and Capacitor native dependencies.
- Prefer shared mocks in `setupTests` for Capacitor plugins.

## Style
- Prefer accessible queries: `getByRole`, `getByLabelText`, `getByText`.
- Keep tests deterministic and isolated.
- Assert outcomes, not internal store/hook wiring.
- Colocate unit tests next to the unit under test (`ComponentName.test.tsx`).
- Keep Playwright e2e focused on critical user journeys, not exhaustive UI permutations.
- Fail tests on unexpected console errors when practical.
